                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "An atmospheric exploration game that really stayed with me.\nThe puzzles can be quite obscure and don’t follow typical game logic, which can be frustrating, but also fits the overall design. It’s closer to a walking sim than an action game—the combat is there, but it’s not the focus.\nWhat makes it work is the atmosphere. The ship feels small but believable, and the story told through logs and notes is engaging, even if it never gives clear answers.\nIt’s a minimalist experience, both in mechanics and scope, but for its short length the atmosphere carries it all the way through. Not for everyone, but definitely worth it if you enjoy slow, mysterious exploration.",
